       " (HELP SET SOUND) come with it.  SET REALISM ENABLED and DISABLED are\n"
       " only allowed while no disk or tape unit is attached.  SET SOUND\n"
-      " ENABLED and SET SOUND DISABLED do the same (older name).\n"
+      " ENABLED and SET SOUND DISABLED do the same (older name).\n\n"
+      " Waiting at the prompt: in the realism mode, a command that starts or\n"
+      " stops a disk spindle or loads, unloads or rewinds a tape waits until\n"
+      " the drive is ready or at rest, as the operator of the real drive\n"
+      " would.  The switch -N returns at once instead, and the drive goes on\n"
+      " in the background:\n\n"
+      "++SET -N RL0 ONLINE\n"
+      "++SET -N TS LOAD\n\n"
+      " This works for the disks RL, RP, HK, RQ, RB and CS (ONLINE, OFFLINE;\n"
+      " RL, RB and CS also LOAD, UNLOAD) and the tapes TS (LOAD, UNLOAD,\n"
+      " ONLINE, OFFLINE, REWIND) and TQ (LOAD, UNLOAD).\n"
+      " SHOW <unit> SPINDLE (disks) or SHOW <unit> TRANSPORT (tapes) shows\n"
+      " how far it has got.  A guest that uses the unit meanwhile finds it not\n"
+      " ready, as on the real hardware.  The WRU character (Ctrl-E) or Ctrl-C\n"
+      " also ends a wait early; the drive goes on, and a DO script stops.\n"
+      " The commands of each drive are in its own help (e.g. HELP RL).\n"
 #define HLP_SET_SOUND "*Commands SET Sound"
       "3Sound\n"
       " Sound output with SDL2 audio: system sounds (power relay, fans), unit\n"
       " loops (spindles) and events (seeks), in the realism mode (HELP SET\n"
       " REALISM).  Without SDL2 or without an audio device, sounds are\n"
-      " silently ignored.\n\n"
+      " silently ignored.  How to get a disk or tape ready without waiting\n"
+      " (SET -N) is in HELP SET REALISM.\n\n"
       "+SET SOUND ENABLED            the same as SET REALISM ENABLED\n"
       "+SET SOUND DISABLED           the same as SET REALISM DISABLED\n"
       "+SET SOUND VOLUME=n           set the master volume (0..200 %%)\n"
